package local:bad;

// A record with no fields, which is not this tool turning something away:
// `wit-parser` accepts the declaration and the component model has no type
// for it, so `wasm-tools` refuses an assembled component with "record type
// must have at least one field". The gate says so here, where the field
// list is still on screen.
//
// The *representation* is not the problem: a nullary constructor is an
// immediate, which is what every `enum` case already is, and the ABI
// flattens this record to no core values at all. It is the component type
// that cannot be written.
world w {
  use certirocq:abi/errors@0.1.0.{error};
  record nothing { }
  export id: func(n: nothing) -> result<nothing, error>;
}
